 wform?usp=header\n\nThe Creative Writing Program is pleased to announce a 
 reading with Stegner Fellows in Poetry and Fiction: Daniel Lurie and Kater
 ina Ivanov Prado. \n\nThis event is open to Stanford affiliates and the ge
 neral public. Registration is encouraged but not required. Register here\n
 \n____\n\nDaniel Lurie is a Jewish\, rural writer\, from eastern Montana. 
 He holds an MFA in Poetry from the University of Idaho and is co-editor of
  Outskirts Literary Journal. His work has appeared or is forthcoming in Pl
 eiades\, Gulf Coast\, RHINO\, Adroit\, The Iowa Review\, Poetry Northwest\
 , and other publications. Daniel won the 2026 Mississippi Review Prize\, P
 inch’s Literary Award\, and phoebe’s Greg Grummer Poetry Contest\, sel
 ected by Diane Seuss. He served as the 2025-2026 Ronald Wallace Poetry Fel
 low at the University of Wisconsin-Madison. Find him at danielluriepoetry.
 com \n\nKaterina Ivanov Prado received an MFA from the University of Arizo
 na and a Ph.D. in Literature and Creative Writing from the University of H
 ouston. Her work has appeared in Narrative\, Brevity\, Catapult\, The Rump
 us\, and Joyland\, and has won The Masters Review Emerging Fiction Award\,
  the Narrative Story Contest\, and the AWP Intro Journals Award\, as well 
 as received support from the Elizabeth George Foundation\, VCCA\, Inprint 
 Houston\, Reese’s Book Club\, and the Bread Loaf Writers Conference.
